    {
      "id": 229873,
      "name": "KateWalker",
      "username": "TakeWalker",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-03-03T12:59:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This was a slog, but Writhe is so clutch against Spite. It just took forever to get the Umbral Siphon out, and once I did? Kinda didn't need it. The trick is to use it when he's about to flip, because the advanced rules let him heal a ton. But mostly, this was about having two (or three) characters who can reduce damage dealt without actually having to deal damage themselves, so that you rarely have to take a hit. The environment is a non-issue once Mindphyre comes out, though I love how you start with All According to Plan and it's kind of a trap.</p>\n<p>And don't forget, Sky-Scraper is also clutch against Spite and just needs to spam Links at all times. Only don't mix the ones that prevent his damage with the ones that make him hit himself, you will feel really dumb when those interfere with each other, not that I would know what that's like. c.c;;;</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:44.153Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 2,
      "readers_count": 1,
      "score": 0.4,
